    {
      "doc_id": "a8527b4b-6de3-4b00-ac6f-9ee3c54c6d7b",
      "role": "user",
      "task_item": "",
      "content": "Projects must have a ticket service where other projects can place a ticket via llm models tools.\nIn this way a project can request a change on a child project or in a read/write linked project.\nThe ticket service will have tools for: create, update, query, abandon ticket.\n\nBusiness case:\nWe have project codx-junior-cloud that is a SaaS platform to offer hosted codx-junior services. During the development of codx-junior-cloud we detect an error, a new feature or need a change in the codx-junior projetc. Instead manage the change directly in the codebase, codx-junior-cloud will place a ticket to codx-junior ticket service receiving an id that can be use to query, update, manage. The ticket is a chat so project's can communicate.\n\nIn this way each project has full control on how to process the ticket queue reviewing, accepting/rejecting the ticket, scheduling or implementing inmediately, assigning the profiles, requesting human review, etc\n\nImplement full ticketing system\n  ",
